From: Bruno Verachten <gounthar@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] xen-cmdline: keep other arguments when given several keys

_filter_args() loops over the keys for every argument, so with
match=False an argument is kept once for each key it does not match.
With two or more keys, --set-xen and --delete-xen (and the dom0
variants) duplicate every other argument, and keep the very argument
being replaced, since it does not match the other key:

  --set-xen dom0_mem=2048M loglvl=all on "sched=null dom0_mem=1536M"
  gives "sched=null sched=null dom0_mem=1536M dom0_mem=2048M loglvl=all"

Keep or drop each argument once, depending on whether any key matches.
With one key the result is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Bruno Verachten <gounthar@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/common/opt/xensource/libexec/xen-cmdline
+++ b/src/common/opt/xensource/libexec/xen-cmdline
@@ -25,9 +25,8 @@
     return arg.startswith(key + "=") or arg == key
 
 def _filter_args(keys, args, match=True):
-    if match:
-        return [arg for arg in args for key in keys if _match_arg(key, arg)]
-    return [arg for arg in args for key in keys if not _match_arg(key, arg)]
+    return [arg for arg in args
+            if any(_match_arg(key, arg) for key in keys) == match]
 
 def get_xen_args(b, keys):
     """Get xen args matching ks"""
